.TH "XWIISHOW" 1 "August 2026" "WiiLand" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
xwiishow \- inspect and test connected Wii Remote devices
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xwiishow
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B xwiishow list
.br
.B xwiishow
.I positive-ordinal
.br
.B xwiishow
.I /sys/path/to/device
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xwiishow
lists Wii Remote devices or opens one in an interactive ncurses interface.
The
.B list
form writes one tab-separated ordinal and absolute sysfs path per line.
It does not require a terminal, so its output can be redirected or piped.
.
.PP
The interactive form accepts exactly one selector: a positive device ordinal
from
.BR "xwiishow list" ,
or an absolute device path below
.BR /sys .
Zero, negative, malformed, overflowing, or trailing-character ordinals are
rejected, as are extra arguments.
Before starting ncurses,
.B xwiishow
prints the resolved path in this form:
.
.nf
Using Wii Remote: /sys/path/to/device
.fi
.
.PP
Interactive use requires terminal devices on both standard input and standard
output, a usable
.B TERM
value, and a terminal at least 80 columns by 24 lines.
It is display-server neutral: it does not connect to X11 or Wayland.
Press
.B q
to quit.
Run
.B "xwiishow --help"
for the complete keyboard command list.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit successfully.
.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Readable input-device access is sufficient for monitoring buttons, sensors,
and extensions.
.B xwiishow
continues opening readable interfaces when optional writable access is denied.
Rumble and LED controls are shown as unavailable when their input device or
sysfs LED attributes cannot be written.
.
.PP
Access is normally granted through the active session's device ACLs or local
udev policy.
If input cannot be read, check the ACLs on the corresponding
.B /dev/input/event*
nodes and the system's udev rules.
If an LED cannot be changed, check write access to its sysfs
.B brightness
attribute.
Running the entire program as root is neither required nor recommended.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices; this form is suitable for a pipeline:
.
.nf
.B $ xwiishow list
1	/sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
.fi
.
.PP
Open the first listed device:
.
.nf
.B $ xwiishow 1
Using Wii Remote: /sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
<ncurses interface headed "WIILAND SHOW">
.fi
.
.PP
The absolute path printed by
.B list
may be passed instead of its ordinal:
.
.nf
.B $ xwiishow /sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
Using Wii Remote: /sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
<ncurses interface headed "WIILAND SHOW">
.fi
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero after explicit help, a successful listing, or a normally closed
interactive session.
Returns nonzero for invalid arguments, an unresolved device, insufficient
read access, terminal setup or restoration failure, or an interactive runtime
failure.
.
